WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.034
-Hi, I'm Seth Meyers.

00:00:02.034 --> 00:00:03.402
The crisis our country
is going through

00:00:03.402 --> 00:00:05.170
is at its heart about
anger and frustration

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:06.405
in the black community

00:00:06.405 --> 00:00:08.641
over years of mistreatment
by law enforcement.

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:10.944
This week, as Americans
came together to protest,

00:00:10.944 --> 00:00:13.679
we opened each show with
"Late Night" writer Amber Ruffin

00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:15.315
telling her personal stories
about her interactions

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:16.516
with the police.

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:17.917
They're profoundly powerful.

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:19.452
They're profoundly
eye-opening.

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:22.221
We gathered all four here.

00:00:22.221 --> 00:00:23.856
-Let me tell you a story.

00:00:23.856 --> 00:00:28.194
So, once when I was a teenager,
I was brand-new to driving,

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:30.663
and I dropped my friend off
at work.

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:32.399
And I'm coming back home,

00:00:32.399 --> 00:00:34.500
and I'm in morning
rush-hour traffic,

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.236
and everybody is going
over the speed limit.

00:00:37.236 --> 00:00:40.707
I think it's like 40,
and everyone is going 50.

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:43.509
And I hate it
because I'm new to driving.

00:00:43.509 --> 00:00:45.011
It's too scary.

00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:49.315
When I slow down, it disrupts
traffic, so I speed up to 45.

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:50.750
That's five miles
over the speed limit.

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:53.019
That's as fast
as I'm willing to go.

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:54.954
And I know I'm going too slow,

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:57.156
and I'm in an unfamiliar
part of town

00:00:57.156 --> 00:00:58.991
and people are whizzing by me.

00:00:58.991 --> 00:01:02.795
So to make myself feel better,
I turn on Busta Rhymes,

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:07.399
and I friggin' blast it so that,
you know, I can calm down.

00:01:07.399 --> 00:01:10.436
And blasting Busta Rhymes
is something that I recommend

00:01:10.436 --> 00:01:13.706
if you're a teenager
who is unsure of themselves.

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:16.743
So, I get to a good pace,
and I start feeling normal.

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:20.146
And just then,
I encounter a speed trap.

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:22.515
And no one is slowing down.

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:26.519
We are all speeding,
me least of all.

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:30.823
So, to my right,
there is an old, white cop

00:01:30.823 --> 00:01:32.425
standing on
the side of the road.

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:36.228
And out of these tens of cars,
he sees a young, black person

00:01:36.228 --> 00:01:40.733
driving a purple car
blasting rap music.

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:44.036
And he chooses me.
And he's screaming at me.

00:01:44.036 --> 00:01:47.440
He is shouting
as if I have murdered someone.

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:51.144
Like, on a scale of 1 to 10,
he is at a 27.

00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:54.013
And he goes, "Pull the car over!

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:58.084
Pull the goddamn car over
right now, mother [bleep]!"

00:01:58.084 --> 00:02:00.286
That is what this cop
is screaming at me,

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:05.224
and I think, "This is how I die.
This man is going to kill me."

00:02:05.224 --> 00:02:07.827
And I start crying.

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:11.730
I am bawling,
because I am 100% sure

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:14.000
that this man is going to

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.569
drag me out of my car,
beat me to death,

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:19.872
and, you know, tomorrow on the
news, everyone will be like,

00:02:19.872 --> 00:02:23.243
"She didn't seem angry,
but who knows?"

00:02:23.243 --> 00:02:26.111
So, I pull over, and I stop.

00:02:26.111 --> 00:02:29.649
He goes, "Pull over
the [bleep] car! [Bleep]!"

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:31.918
He's shouting. It does not stop.

00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:35.921
So, he gets up to the car, and
he puts his hand on the door.

00:02:35.921 --> 00:02:38.924
And he goes to start yelling,
and he sees me.

00:02:38.924 --> 00:02:44.663
He sees a teenage girl
whose face is wet with tears.

00:02:44.663 --> 00:02:46.165
And I'm just braced,

00:02:46.165 --> 00:02:48.801
trying to think of all the good
things that have happened

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:51.003
in my life so that
I get to heaven thankful,

00:02:51.003 --> 00:02:52.438
instead of angry.

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:54.374
And he looks me in the eye.

00:02:54.374 --> 00:02:59.845
And he drops it and goes,
"Oh, okay, well, just --

00:02:59.845 --> 00:03:02.682
It's okay.
Just let me have your I.D."

00:03:02.682 --> 00:03:04.317
And, you know, he's taken aback.

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:07.153
He goes from a 27
to a negative 2.

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:12.124
His whole demeanor changes,
and it's as if

00:03:12.124 --> 00:03:17.430
he wasn't the guy
who was just screaming at me.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.766
He's a totally different guy.

00:03:19.766 --> 00:03:21.233
All of a sudden, he's nice.

00:03:21.233 --> 00:03:26.772
So I give him my I.D.

00:03:26.772 --> 00:03:29.808
He sends me on my way
without a warning,

00:03:29.808 --> 00:03:34.280
because once he saw
a teenage girl...

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.783
shouting was no longer fun?

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:39.318
Look, I have a thousand stories
like this.

00:03:39.318 --> 00:03:41.687
The cops have pulled a gun
on me.

00:03:41.687 --> 00:03:45.158
The cops have followed me
to my own home.

00:03:45.158 --> 00:03:51.697
And every black person I know
has a few stories like that.

00:03:51.697 --> 00:03:54.900
Many have more than a few.

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:57.402
Black people
leave the house every day

00:03:57.402 --> 00:03:59.639
knowing that at any time,

00:03:59.639 --> 00:04:01.841
we could get murdered
by the police.

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:03.376
It's a lot.

00:04:03.376 --> 00:04:06.912
And sometimes
when you see news footage

00:04:06.912 --> 00:04:08.881
like we have seen the past week

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:12.585
and you hear people chalking
it up to a few bad apples

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:15.721
instead of how corrupt
an entire system is,

00:04:15.721 --> 00:04:18.424
it becomes too much.

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:21.894
And that's what I wanted to say.

00:04:21.894 --> 00:04:23.863
And I wanted to end this
with something hopeful

00:04:23.863 --> 00:04:25.765
to, you know,
provide some comfort,

00:04:25.765 --> 00:04:29.669
but maybe it's time
to get uncomfortable.

00:04:31.303 --> 00:04:33.105
Last night, I told you a story

00:04:33.105 --> 00:04:35.474
about an encounter I had
with police.

00:04:35.474 --> 00:04:38.410
Now let me tell you
another story.

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:42.281
One time, a few years ago,
I was living in Amsterdam.

00:04:42.281 --> 00:04:43.949
And I flew to Chicago
for the weekend

00:04:43.949 --> 00:04:45.717
to visit some friends
who live there.

00:04:45.717 --> 00:04:49.455
When I got there, my friend Jeff
and I hopped in his car

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:52.492
and headed out to pick up
our friend Krasney,

00:04:52.492 --> 00:04:53.959
who just so happened to live

00:04:53.959 --> 00:04:58.563
next to the alley
behind the police station.

00:04:58.563 --> 00:05:00.666
So, Jeff parks his car

00:05:00.666 --> 00:05:02.869
at the gas station
at the end of the alley

00:05:02.869 --> 00:05:05.438
so that I can run out,
go pick up Krasney,

00:05:05.438 --> 00:05:07.873
and take her back to the car.

00:05:07.873 --> 00:05:11.110
I'm freaking thrilled.
I hadn't seen her in years.

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:15.014
So, we were all going to
go have dinner and catch up.

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:17.449
Now, I get out of the car
and go down the alley.

00:05:17.449 --> 00:05:20.453
And because Jeff is watching me,
I skip down the alley

00:05:20.453 --> 00:05:23.021
to her house to make him laugh,
you know?

00:05:23.021 --> 00:05:25.257
But little did I know

00:05:25.257 --> 00:05:28.728
skipping down a police-station
alley is a big no-no.

00:05:28.728 --> 00:05:31.297
Because I end up
skipping towards a cop car

00:05:31.297 --> 00:05:34.300
that's driving at me
down the alley.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:36.001
The sirens go off.

00:05:36.001 --> 00:05:39.004
A cop gets out,
and his gun is drawn.

00:05:39.004 --> 00:05:41.174
And he goes, "Put your hands
on the hood of the car!

00:05:41.174 --> 00:05:43.509
Put your hands on the hood!"

00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:46.179
This man is furious.

00:05:46.179 --> 00:05:50.416
I comply,
and his partner pats me down.

00:05:50.416 --> 00:05:52.818
Now, this man is livid.

00:05:52.818 --> 00:05:54.721
It makes no sense.

00:05:54.721 --> 00:05:58.857
His anger level towards me
is insane.

00:05:58.857 --> 00:06:02.160
I am a young, adorable, delight

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:04.263
literally skipping
down the street,

00:06:04.263 --> 00:06:06.332
and I've infuriated him.

00:06:06.332 --> 00:06:10.635
So, this man asked me,
"Where are you coming from?"

00:06:10.635 --> 00:06:12.972
And I go, "Amsterdam."

00:06:12.972 --> 00:06:15.441
Now, this answer enrages him.

00:06:15.441 --> 00:06:17.443
And he goes, "No, where are you
coming from right now?

00:06:17.443 --> 00:06:19.044
Where are you coming from?"

00:06:19.044 --> 00:06:24.216
And I go, "From the airport.
From a flight. From Amsterdam."

00:06:24.216 --> 00:06:26.251
And he goes, "Why in the world

00:06:26.251 --> 00:06:28.454
are you running down
this alley?!"

00:06:28.454 --> 00:06:31.290
I go, "I'm not running.
I'm skipping.

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:32.991
I'm happy to be back in town.

00:06:32.991 --> 00:06:36.529
I'm going to pick up
my friend Krasney

00:06:36.529 --> 00:06:38.464
and take her back to Jeff's car,

00:06:38.464 --> 00:06:40.632
and we're all going to
go catch up over dinner."

00:06:40.632 --> 00:06:43.769
And I remember,
"Oh, thank God. Jeff is here."

00:06:43.769 --> 00:06:45.971
I gesture back to Jeff.

00:06:45.971 --> 00:06:50.476
Jeff is standing outside of his
car just watching all of this.

00:06:50.476 --> 00:06:56.148
And he goes --
So, the cop and I see Jeff.

00:06:56.148 --> 00:06:59.519
And thank God Jeff
didn't come running up to us,

00:06:59.519 --> 00:07:02.154
because he could have
gotten us both shot.

00:07:02.154 --> 00:07:06.425
But the cop sees that Jeff,
a white man, has seen all this,

00:07:06.425 --> 00:07:11.830
and he changes his attitude
with the quickness.

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:14.933
He's suddenly professional
instead of antagonistic.

00:07:14.933 --> 00:07:19.071
And he tells me
that I was wrong for running.

00:07:19.071 --> 00:07:22.508
And it takes everything in me
not to tell him

00:07:22.508 --> 00:07:25.811
that if I wanted
to run down the alley,

00:07:25.811 --> 00:07:28.848
that would be perfectly legal.

00:07:28.848 --> 00:07:31.183
So, instead,
I also gently remind him

00:07:31.183 --> 00:07:33.486
that I was not running,
I was skipping.

00:07:33.486 --> 00:07:36.488
So, the cop gets in his car,
and he leaves.

00:07:36.488 --> 00:07:40.292
And I walk to Krasney's house.

00:07:40.292 --> 00:07:43.362
I get her.
We take her back to the car.

00:07:43.362 --> 00:07:46.499
Jeff is really bothered
by what happened, but I'm not.

00:07:46.499 --> 00:07:49.335
[Bleep] That man could have
shot me in a second.

00:07:49.335 --> 00:07:52.872
People who know me would be
running around talking about,

00:07:52.872 --> 00:07:55.407
"Attacking an officer
doesn't seem like

00:07:55.407 --> 00:07:59.044
something Amber would do,
but the officer said she did,

00:07:59.044 --> 00:08:02.215
so that has to be
what happened."

00:08:02.215 --> 00:08:06.385
So...

00:08:06.385 --> 00:08:09.622
The second I see Krasney,
I feel a lot better.

00:08:09.622 --> 00:08:13.092
And we go, and we have
a lot of fun that night.

00:08:13.092 --> 00:08:16.495
And if you think about it, it's
kind of my duty to have fun

00:08:16.495 --> 00:08:22.834
because at any time, I could
get murdered by the police.

00:08:22.834 --> 00:08:28.975
Now, every black person I know
has stories like that.

00:08:28.975 --> 00:08:30.642
[ Sighs ]

00:08:30.642 --> 00:08:33.546
It's crazy that people don't
run around telling everyone

00:08:33.546 --> 00:08:35.047
these stories all the time.

00:08:35.047 --> 00:08:37.182
But there's this unspoken rule

00:08:37.182 --> 00:08:40.853
that black people are
supposed to take it in stride.

00:08:40.853 --> 00:08:45.223
Can you imagine having
someone pull a gun on you

00:08:45.223 --> 00:08:49.428
and being expected
to take it in stride?

00:08:49.428 --> 00:08:54.600
Now imagine a bunch of incidents
like that over one lifetime,

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:58.371
multiply that by
43 million African-Americans,

00:08:58.371 --> 00:09:02.308
and that is why things
are like this right now.

00:09:02.308 --> 00:09:04.075
That is why people are angry.

00:09:04.075 --> 00:09:08.381
And if you're not angry...
why not?

00:09:10.516 --> 00:09:12.584
The last two days,
I've told stories about

00:09:12.584 --> 00:09:14.654
my run-ins with the cops.

00:09:14.654 --> 00:09:16.989
Today I'm going to tell you
a story about

00:09:16.989 --> 00:09:18.757
a run-in with the cops.

00:09:18.757 --> 00:09:23.862
Okay, I was living in Chicago,
and my friend Anthony

00:09:23.862 --> 00:09:26.531
had just left my house.

00:09:26.531 --> 00:09:30.802
Now, he goes out the door,
across the porch,

00:09:30.802 --> 00:09:34.072
down the stairs, gets on
his bike and rides away.

00:09:34.072 --> 00:09:37.342
I shut the door, I go inside,
I change into my pajamas.

00:09:37.342 --> 00:09:38.744
And when I come out of my room,

00:09:38.744 --> 00:09:40.812
I see that
he has left his wallet.

00:09:40.812 --> 00:09:43.649
So I call him.
He comes back to get it.

00:09:43.649 --> 00:09:48.354
I step out onto the porch with
no shoes, in my pajamas.

00:09:48.354 --> 00:09:50.289
And instead of walking to
the end of the porch

00:09:50.289 --> 00:09:53.159
and down the stairs, I just
reach over the side of the porch

00:09:53.159 --> 00:09:54.727
to give him his wallet back.

00:09:54.727 --> 00:10:00.299
So, he rides up on his bicycle
and just lets his bicycle fall

00:10:00.299 --> 00:10:02.534
and then reaches up
to get his wallet.

00:10:02.534 --> 00:10:05.170
Now, at that moment,
I'm reaching down

00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:09.641
and he's reaching up, a cop car
pulls up, flashes its lights.

00:10:09.641 --> 00:10:13.212
The cop gets out, and she's
like, "Hold it right there!

00:10:13.212 --> 00:10:14.847
We gotcha!"

00:10:14.847 --> 00:10:17.049
I'm like, "Okay."

00:10:17.049 --> 00:10:20.085
Now, everything she says to us

00:10:20.085 --> 00:10:23.388
she says with her hand
on her gun.

00:10:23.388 --> 00:10:27.259
Now, I'm terrified,
because while I'm a black lady,

00:10:27.259 --> 00:10:30.663
Anthony is a black man,

00:10:30.663 --> 00:10:35.167
and this cop is a tiny,
little white lady.

00:10:35.167 --> 00:10:38.170
Now, I'm scared.

00:10:38.170 --> 00:10:39.471
Anthony's scared.

00:10:39.471 --> 00:10:42.641
I've had a lot of run-ins
with the cops at this point.

00:10:42.641 --> 00:10:44.610
And isn't it hilarious that

00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:47.312
when people say
"run-ins with the cops,"

00:10:47.312 --> 00:10:49.315
they mean they got caught
doing something?

00:10:49.315 --> 00:10:53.952
But when I say it, I just mean
being a person that they bother?

00:10:53.952 --> 00:10:57.022
Okay, so, this cop says,

00:10:57.022 --> 00:10:59.892
"Why were you guys
running from the police?"

00:10:59.892 --> 00:11:01.627
And we're like, "We're not.

00:11:01.627 --> 00:11:03.862
I'm not running anywhere.
I live here."

00:11:03.862 --> 00:11:05.597
And she's like, "Okay."

00:11:05.597 --> 00:11:08.233
Meanwhile, I'm like,
bitch, I have no shoes on.

00:11:08.233 --> 00:11:09.401
I don't say that.

00:11:09.401 --> 00:11:13.405
I say, "I'm in my pajamas
with no shoes on,"

00:11:13.405 --> 00:11:15.608
and she goes,
"Let me see both your I.D.'s."

00:11:15.608 --> 00:11:18.210
I go, "Okay, but to get my I.D.,

00:11:18.210 --> 00:11:21.113
I have to go
in the house, okay?"

00:11:21.113 --> 00:11:22.481
And she's like, "Fine."

00:11:22.481 --> 00:11:26.918
So I go in the house, and
the whole time I'm in the house,

00:11:26.918 --> 00:11:30.089
she's asking Anthony
a million questions.

00:11:30.089 --> 00:11:32.324
So, I come up.
I give her my I.D.

00:11:32.324 --> 00:11:34.627
She says,
"This address is from Nebraska."

00:11:34.627 --> 00:11:36.128
And she's right.

00:11:36.128 --> 00:11:40.432
I go, "Oh, yeah, I don't have
a new Chicago I.D. yet."

00:11:40.432 --> 00:11:43.335
And she goes, "Well, then I need
proof you live here.

00:11:43.335 --> 00:11:44.904
Go get some mail."

00:11:44.904 --> 00:11:46.938
Now, this is where the story
takes a turn,

00:11:46.938 --> 00:11:50.542
and I can't describe it exactly
except to say

00:11:50.542 --> 00:11:55.180
now she has unsnapped that thing
that holds your gun in place

00:11:55.180 --> 00:11:58.384
and is holding on
to her gun tighter.

00:11:58.384 --> 00:12:01.187
So, I go inside
and I'm freaking out

00:12:01.187 --> 00:12:03.355
because she's going to shoot
my friend Anthony

00:12:03.355 --> 00:12:05.791
for just being bigger than her?

00:12:05.791 --> 00:12:08.360
So I go in,
and I tear up the house,

00:12:08.360 --> 00:12:10.962
looking for a piece of mail
with my name on it,

00:12:10.962 --> 00:12:13.231
but I just moved there,
so I don't really have any!

00:12:13.231 --> 00:12:16.568
So, I go, I get the mail,
I come out,

00:12:16.568 --> 00:12:21.206
and for some reason,
she has calmed down.

00:12:21.206 --> 00:12:22.741
I give her the mail.

00:12:22.741 --> 00:12:26.344
She looks at the mail, and she
looks at us and she goes,

00:12:26.344 --> 00:12:29.949
"Okay, from now on, when I tell
you to stop, you stop."

00:12:29.949 --> 00:12:33.786
Now, remember, she's never
told us to stop anything.

00:12:33.786 --> 00:12:35.254
And I look at Anthony like,

00:12:35.254 --> 00:12:37.957
"Oh, my God, are you going to
handle this cop lying on us?

00:12:37.957 --> 00:12:41.326
And he looks at me and he looks
at the cop and he goes, "Okay."

00:12:41.326 --> 00:12:43.662
I look at him and I go, "Okay,"

00:12:43.662 --> 00:12:46.799
and we live to get harassed
another day!

00:12:46.799 --> 00:12:50.002
Because that's the kind of thing
you have to do

00:12:50.002 --> 00:12:51.937
to stay alive when you're black.

00:12:51.937 --> 00:12:58.410
You have to let the police
lie to you at your own house.

00:12:58.410 --> 00:13:00.479
That's it. That's my story.

00:13:00.479 --> 00:13:03.716
We used to open this show
with fun jokes,

00:13:03.716 --> 00:13:05.584
but for the last three days,

00:13:05.584 --> 00:13:09.054
we've opened this show
with stories about me

00:13:09.054 --> 00:13:11.457
getting mistreated by the cops.

00:13:11.457 --> 00:13:18.030
And if you're tired of hearing
these stories, do something!

00:13:19.531 --> 00:13:22.901
For the past three days,
we have opened "Late Night"

00:13:22.901 --> 00:13:27.673
with me telling a story
about run-ins with the cops.

00:13:27.673 --> 00:13:30.843
And tonight, I'm out of stories.

00:13:30.843 --> 00:13:32.244
Just kidding.
I have more.

00:13:32.244 --> 00:13:35.881
A few years ago, I'm in the car
with my white friend.

00:13:35.881 --> 00:13:38.984
He is a white man in a suit.

00:13:38.984 --> 00:13:41.420
He's just gotten off of work.

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:46.758
Now, I'm in a head-to-toe
velvet outfit because I'm great.

00:13:46.758 --> 00:13:49.161
I think I was going to a party,

00:13:49.161 --> 00:13:52.398
so it was like
my favorite party outfit.

00:13:52.398 --> 00:13:55.400
I still remember that thing.
It was beautiful.

00:13:55.400 --> 00:13:59.738
It was not that late at night.

00:13:59.738 --> 00:14:02.241
So, we're at a truck stop,

00:14:02.241 --> 00:14:07.880
seeing if my friend's dad,
who is a truck driver, is there.

00:14:07.880 --> 00:14:11.250
We're driving slowly
along the semitrucks,

00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:14.353
looking
for his dad's license plate.

00:14:14.353 --> 00:14:18.890
So I can see why
we may have seemed suspicious.

00:14:18.890 --> 00:14:22.160
And a cop comes up,
and he taps on the window.

00:14:22.160 --> 00:14:23.896
And I'm like, "Frick!"

00:14:23.896 --> 00:14:26.398
I have been harassed
for doing nothing.

00:14:26.398 --> 00:14:28.200
I'm sure this guy
is going to get us.

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:32.470
My friend rolls down the window,
and the cop is super nice.

00:14:32.470 --> 00:14:34.706
Now, I had never been stopped
by a cop

00:14:34.706 --> 00:14:37.443
while a white man was around.

00:14:37.443 --> 00:14:40.245
And the respect this cop had

00:14:40.245 --> 00:14:44.983
for this white man
in this suit, man, I --

00:14:44.983 --> 00:14:48.620
this cop wants to know
what in the world we are doing,

00:14:48.620 --> 00:14:50.355
and he asked politely.

00:14:50.355 --> 00:14:54.393
And we tell him,
and he is unsatisfied.

00:14:54.393 --> 00:14:55.927
He goes, "I stopped you

00:14:55.927 --> 00:14:59.898
because there's been
a lot of prostitution."

00:14:59.898 --> 00:15:04.135
[ Laughing ] And I go,
"Oh, I'm not a prostitute."

00:15:04.135 --> 00:15:08.273
And this cop has never believed
anything less.

00:15:08.273 --> 00:15:13.945
He looks at our I.D.s,
and he asks us more questions.

00:15:13.945 --> 00:15:18.516
And my white friend
is getting annoyed at this cop.

00:15:18.516 --> 00:15:19.918
And the cop can tell.

00:15:19.918 --> 00:15:21.220
But I'm like,

00:15:21.220 --> 00:15:24.022
"Oh, my gosh, please
just calm down and be cool."

00:15:24.022 --> 00:15:25.824
My friend says to the cop --
he goes,

00:15:25.824 --> 00:15:28.827
"You have nothing.
You have to let us go."

00:15:28.827 --> 00:15:33.532
And I'm like,
"You just got me killed!"

00:15:33.532 --> 00:15:37.269
But the cop goes...
[Sighs]

00:15:37.269 --> 00:15:41.974
"Okay, but you have to leave."

00:15:41.974 --> 00:15:43.142
[ Laughing ] Ok--
And then that was it.

00:15:43.142 --> 00:15:44.876
My friend was like,
"She's not a prostitute!"

00:15:44.876 --> 00:15:46.311
And I was like, "Oh, shut up.

00:15:46.311 --> 00:15:49.214
Hey, we're going.
Thank you. Goodbye."

00:15:49.214 --> 00:15:51.249
Y'all, the respect this cop

00:15:51.249 --> 00:15:54.953
just automatically had
for my friend --

00:15:54.953 --> 00:15:57.055
I'll never forget seeing it.

00:15:57.055 --> 00:15:58.891
So, that's it.

00:15:58.891 --> 00:16:00.759
That's my story.

00:16:00.759 --> 00:16:02.427
Alright.

00:16:02.427 --> 00:16:07.299
So, for the past 10 days,

00:16:07.299 --> 00:16:11.903
the George Floyd protests
were worldwide.

00:16:11.903 --> 00:16:15.407
Like, hundreds of thousands
of people

00:16:15.407 --> 00:16:19.111
all over the country,
all over the world,

00:16:19.111 --> 00:16:25.784
saw yet another video of a man
being murdered in cold blood

00:16:25.784 --> 00:16:27.586
and rose up.

00:16:27.586 --> 00:16:31.189
People all over the world
took to the streets

00:16:31.189 --> 00:16:33.692
because they believe that

00:16:33.692 --> 00:16:36.327
black people deserve
better treatment

00:16:36.327 --> 00:16:39.864
than we have been getting.

00:16:39.864 --> 00:16:41.433
[ Breathes sharply ]

00:16:41.433 --> 00:16:44.068
And, you know, I'm not like,
"Oh, wow, everything's over.

00:16:44.068 --> 00:16:45.404
Everything is fixed."

00:16:45.404 --> 00:16:49.341
But...y'all, I am so shocked

00:16:49.341 --> 00:16:56.281
that so many people showed up
for black people.

00:16:56.281 --> 00:17:03.155
We've been being discriminated
against for fun for years,

00:17:03.155 --> 00:17:09.861
and I didn't think
people cared or saw

00:17:09.861 --> 00:17:14.032
or they knew
and were fine with it.

00:17:14.032 --> 00:17:20.205
For whatever reason,
everyone is fed up, thank God.

00:17:20.205 --> 00:17:22.774
And last night,
Obama held a town hall,

00:17:22.774 --> 00:17:26.678
and he talked
about a comprehensive plan

00:17:26.678 --> 00:17:28.814
with real policies

00:17:28.814 --> 00:17:32.818
that can start saving lives
right now.

00:17:32.818 --> 00:17:34.786
He talked about easy things

00:17:34.786 --> 00:17:37.289
that every police force
in America

00:17:37.289 --> 00:17:39.657
can choose to do this second

00:17:39.657 --> 00:17:42.961
and start saving lives
this minute.

00:17:42.961 --> 00:17:44.295
[ Breathes sharply ]

00:17:44.295 --> 00:17:48.800
This change, if they enact it,
would be great.

00:17:48.800 --> 00:17:54.239
But please don't forget
that it cost us

00:17:54.239 --> 00:17:57.008
not only George Floyd's life,

00:17:57.008 --> 00:18:00.379
but the lives of 11 people

00:18:00.379 --> 00:18:03.715
who have been killed
during these protests,

00:18:03.715 --> 00:18:08.219
including David McAtee...

00:18:08.219 --> 00:18:10.589
Dave Patrick Underwood...

00:18:10.589 --> 00:18:12.257
Chris Beaty...

00:18:12.257 --> 00:18:13.791
Dorian Murrell...

00:18:13.791 --> 00:18:15.927
Italia Kelly...

00:18:15.927 --> 00:18:18.163
Calvin Horton Jr...

00:18:18.163 --> 00:18:19.898
Javar Harrell...

00:18:19.898 --> 00:18:22.034
Victor Cazares...

00:18:22.034 --> 00:18:23.935
Sean Monterrosa...

00:18:23.935 --> 00:18:25.670
David Dorn...

00:18:25.670 --> 00:18:29.540
and from my hometown
of Omaha, Nebraska,

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:31.977
the brave James Scurlock.

00:18:31.977 --> 00:18:35.681
Don't let it cost more lives.

00:18:35.681 --> 00:18:37.682
Vote.

00:18:37.682 --> 00:18:39.184
[Bleep]

00:18:39.184 --> 00:18:41.086
I don't want to do it again.

00:18:41.086 --> 00:18:42.520
Vote.

00:18:42.520 --> 00:18:45.923
Call your representatives.
Unfriend racists.

00:18:45.923 --> 00:18:49.161
And most importantly,

00:18:49.161 --> 00:18:51.763
when you see something,
say something.

00:18:51.763 --> 00:18:53.932
Do something.
Get loud.

00:18:53.932 --> 00:18:57.335
Don't let people get away
with racist crap -- not anymore.

00:18:57.335 --> 00:18:59.404
It's a new day.

